│ patch_description        │ No validator message was captured, so the failure must be inferred from the program       │
│                          │ structure. The original solution uses `std::span`, which requires C++20 and can fail to   │
│                          │ compile under a C++17 contest environment. It also contains a large randomized search and │
│                          │ several partial-simulation paths, increasing the chance of state inconsistency or timeout │
│                          │ despite correctness only requiring a valid sequence.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fix replaces the fragile heuristic machinery with a deterministic simulation. For     │
│                          │ each required box in ascending order, all boxes above it are moved as one block to a      │
│                          │ different stack, then the target box is carried out. This is always legal for the fixed   │
│                          │ `m=10` constraints, uses at most `2*n = 400` operations, and maintains stack positions    │
│                          │ explicitly.                                                                               │
