│ patch_description        │ No validator message was captured, so the failure cannot be tied to one reported invalid  │
│                          │ operation. The original solution used a large randomized beam-search/SA pipeline with     │
│                          │ complex partial-state simulation and a C++20 `std::span` dependency. This unnecessarily   │
│                          │ risks compilation incompatibility, timeout, and state inconsistencies.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fix replaces the heuristic pipeline with a deterministic simulation that always       │
│                          │ produces legal operations. For each required box `1..n`, it moves the suffix above that   │
│                          │ box to a different stack, then immediately carries the box out. Since there are 10        │
│                          │ stacks, a distinct destination always exists. The solution uses at most `2*n = 400`       │
│                          │ operations, safely below the 5000-operation limit.                                        │
