│ patch_description        │ No specific runtime error was captured, so the failure must be handled as a               │
│                          │ validation/robustness issue. The original program relies on a large time-sensitive        │
│                          │ heuristic implementation and C++20 `std::span`; this can fail under a C++17 contest       │
│                          │ compiler and is unnecessarily risky for producing a valid operation sequence.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fix replaces the heuristic search with a deterministic direct simulation. For each    │
│                          │ required box in ascending order, it finds the box, moves the entire suffix above it to a  │
│                          │ different shortest stack, and then carries the required box out. Every move is legal, the │
│                          │ order inside moved blocks is preserved, and at most `2*n` operations are emitted, well    │
│                          │ below 5000.                                                                               │
