│ patch_name               │ future_aware_tiebreak                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Keep the empirically effective shortest-stack rule as the primary criterion, so the       │
│                          │ immediate move cost behavior is unchanged. When several destination stacks have the same  │
│                          │ minimum height, select the one whose smallest remaining box label is largest.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Moving a suffix onto a destination buries every box currently in that destination.        │
│                          │ Therefore, among equally short destinations, burying the stack whose next required box is │
│                          │ furthest in the future is preferable: it is less likely that the just-moved suffix must   │
│                          │ be moved away again soon. This adds future-blocking awareness only as a tie-breaker,      │
│                          │ avoiding the risk of sacrificing the strong minimum-height heuristic for a speculative    │
│                          │ long-term decision.                                                                       │
