│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement directly simulates a guaranteed legal strategy. For each required box     │
│                          │ `v`, it finds the box, moves the entire suffix strictly above it to a different stack,    │
│                          │ then carries out `v`. This always exposes the current smallest remaining box, preserves   │
│                          │ box order during moves, and uses at most `2*n = 400` operations, well below the           │
│                          │ 5000-operation limit. It also avoids the unnecessary C++20 `std::span` dependency.        │
