│ patch_description        │ This approach performs an offline portfolio search instead of committing to one           │
│                          │ destination heuristic. It simulates many complete valid solutions using different         │
│                          │ destination priorities, then outputs the lowest-energy plan found.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Each simulated policy selects a destination by balancing:                                 │
│                          │ - a high minimum remaining label in the destination stack, so boxes needed soon are not   │
│                          │ buried;                                                                                   │
│                          │ - low destination height, reducing future obstruction;                                    │
│                          │ - optional preference for a high top label;                                               │
│                          │ - deterministic small diversification noise to explore structurally different plans.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Because there are only 200 boxes and 10 stacks, hundreds of full simulations are          │
│                          │ inexpensive. The best complete simulated plan is retained, guaranteeing legality while    │
│                          │ usually finding a lower-energy arrangement than a single fixed greedy rule.               │
