│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ latest_needed_destination                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the purely shortest-stack destination rule with a priority based on the smallest  │
│                          │ remaining label in each candidate stack. A stack containing a smaller label will need to  │
│                          │ be accessed sooner, so placing a blocking suffix onto it is likely to create additional   │
│                          │ future moves. Prefer the stack whose minimum label is largest, meaning its next required  │
│                          │ box is furthest in the future. Use stack height only as a tie-breaker to retain the       │
│                          │ useful balancing behavior of the original strategy. This directly improves the expected   │
│                          │ amount of repeatedly moved boxes while preserving the same always-valid ascending-target  │
│                          │ construction.                                                                             │
