│ patch_name               │ rollout_destination_choice                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the purely local “largest minimum label” destination rule with a bounded          │
│                          │ deterministic rollout. For each possible destination, the solver applies the candidate    │
│                          │ move on a trial state, removes the current target, and greedily simulates the next        │
│                          │ several removals. The primary comparison is predicted relocation energy, followed by      │
│                          │ total relocated boxes, maximum stack height, and the urgency of boxes still buried after  │
│                          │ the rollout.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The existing rule protects an urgent destination stack, but cannot distinguish two        │
│                          │ destinations that look equally safe now and create very different blocking patterns       │
│                          │ shortly afterward. Since there are only 10 stacks and 200 boxes, evaluating 9 candidates  │
│                          │ over a short horizon is cheap while providing a materially better placement signal.       │
