│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ destination_rollout                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the purely shortest-stack destination rule with a bounded deterministic rollout.  │
│                          │ For every possible destination, the code simulates the forced move and then simulates the │
│                          │ next several target removals using the existing shortest-stack policy. It selects the     │
│                          │ destination with the lowest simulated future moving energy.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The immediate cost of moving the current suffix is identical for every destination, while │
│                          │ the destination strongly affects which near-future boxes become buried. As a tie-breaker, │
│                          │ an imminent-target penalty prefers not to place the suffix on top of boxes whose labels   │
│                          │ will be needed soon. This preserves the robust baseline behavior while making destination │
│                          │ choices aware of the actual ascending removal order.                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
