│ patch_description        │ Add a small deterministic rollout when evaluating each possible destination stack. The    │
│                          │ current policy only estimates urgency from the minimum label currently in a destination   │
│                          │ stack. This misses whether that placement causes expensive relocations shortly afterward. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For selected additional policies, each candidate destination is temporarily applied and   │
│                          │ the next five removals are simulated using the same destination rule. The candidate is    │
│                          │ penalized by the relocation energy in this short future. This retains the fast policy     │
│                          │ search while making choices aware of near-term stack interactions. Existing zero-depth    │
│                          │ policies remain available unchanged, and several rollout weights are included so the      │
│                          │ final per-instance selection can choose whether and how strongly to trust the forecast.   │
