╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ priority_rollout_stacks                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This program replaces the short, height-restricted lookahead with a priority-aware        │
│                          │ rollout policy.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key idea is that moving a blocking suffix onto a stack does not only affect stack     │
│                          │ height: it buries every box already in the destination stack. Burying a box that will be  │
│                          │ needed soon is much more harmful than burying a large-label box that will only be needed  │
│                          │ far later. The new implementation therefore uses an obstruction potential based on the    │
│                          │ labels currently contained in each candidate destination stack.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For every real move, all possible destination stacks are evaluated. Each candidate is     │
│                          │ simulated through a substantially longer deterministic rollout. During that rollout,      │
│                          │ future suffix moves are selected using the priority-weighted burial potential, and the    │
│                          │ remaining state receives a terminal penalty for near-future boxes that are still deeply   │
│                          │ buried. This combines exact local simulation with a label-aware estimate of delayed       │
│                          │ extraction cost.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The algorithm remains safely within the operation limit: every box is removed once and    │
│                          │ each box causes at most one suffix-moving operation before its removal.                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0496                                                                                   │
